        "content": "I've drafted the graph for the password reset flow. It has five parts: the user, the web app, the users database, and the email service. The edges follow your steps: the user asks for help, the app looks up the account, sends a one-time link by email, the user receives it, and then sets a new password in the app.\n\nMermaid preview:\n\n```\nflowchart LR\n  subgraph backend[\"Your app\"]\n    app[\"Web app\"]\n    users[(\"Users\")]\n  end\n  user([\"User\"])\n  mailer{{\"Email service\"}}\n  user ask@-->|\"Forgot password\"| app\n  app lookup@-->|\"find the account\"| users\n  app send_link@-->|\"one-time link\"| mailer\n  mailer deliver@-->|\"email\"| user\n  user set_password@-->|\"new password\"| app\n```\n\nDoes this graph look right? Should I change any labels or add parts, such as a separate token store or a check that the link has expired? Once you approve it, I'll move on to the story.",
